div.p:
—develop and maintain a “special relationship” with the US, which it sees as the
                    ultimate protector of the Saudi kingdom from external subversion, and as a major
                    source of the technology needed for the kingdom’s development;

—lack of trained manpower, which makes it difficult to staff ministries at home
                    and diplomatic posts abroad with qualified personnel, and tends to concentrate
                    all decision-making responsibilities on the top leadership;
